# Diffusers models

Read `.ai/models.md` before editing. Don't invent a parallel style.

- Single-file layout: attention, blocks, and RoPE live in `transformer_<name>.py` (or import / `# Copied from` a shared layer).
- Load weights only via `from_pretrained` / `from_single_file` — no `hf_hub_download` or custom `from_pretrained`.
- No new mandatory dependency (e.g. `einops`) without discussion.
- Don't declare `attention_mask` in `forward` if you ignore it.

```python
# ❌ BAD
hidden_states = F.scaled_dot_product_attention(query, key, value)

# ✅ GOOD
hidden_states = dispatch_attention_fn(
    query, key, value, attn_mask=attention_mask,
    backend=self._attention_backend, parallel_config=self._parallel_config,
)
```

The `Attention` class and its processor stay in the model file. Processor uses `dispatch_attention_fn`. See `.ai/models.md` (Attention pattern).
